<title>USA: NO DAMAGING COLD INDICATED FOR BRAZIL COFFEE - WSC.</title>
<headline>NO DAMAGING COLD INDICATED FOR BRAZIL COFFEE - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cool weather is expected this week in the coffee-growing areas of Brazil, but no damaging cold is indicated, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Monday.</p>
<p>The forecast is for dry weather Monday and Tuesday, with lows of 48-64 F and the coolest conditions in the hills. Wednesday to Friday will be dry and mild, WSC said.</p>
<p>East-central Brazil was dry on Sunday, with lows of 45-60 F.</p>
</text>
